From b82c7bf0184644755c626fc480c9e6d451ee7d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Joldersma <bennidhamma@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:25:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] [Views] Blur behind translucent menus; grayscale text on
 glass

- MenuScrollViewContainer asks the window system to blur behind the
  menu's rounded body whenever the menu background is translucent
  (e.g. menus of glass browser windows), via the new
  PlatformWindow::SetBackgroundBlurRegion().
- Labels that are not painted onto an opaque surface fall back to
  grayscale antialiasing instead of subpixel rendering, which samples
  the (transparent) color channels underneath.
- frame_view_utils_linux gains helpers to rasterize a rounded window
  shape into a pixel region and to subtract rects from a region.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
